 should be on things  like the customs union can you say  definitively when the UK will be leaving  the customs union under your  government's plan as a prime minister  said we will leave the customs union we  leave the European Union at the  obviously next year that we may have the  implementation period would that will be  delivered as we said we would and  there's no change the position of prime  ministers taken and when you asked on  Friday if we'd be staying in the customs  union until 2023 you said that cabinet  would be making some decisions on that  so had those decisions now been made  actually what I was talking about was  the fact I was being asked about the  decisions and the conversations cabinet  having linked to the meeting last week  which I wasn't at not least I was out on  the campaign trail myself on Wednesday  and I'm not on that committee but  cabinet meets on Tuesday Konami's every  Tuesday and we discuss him what we  in terms of that final deal the we will  negotiate and as my position has been  the same from the very beginning we are  is right that we respect the decision  that was made in that referendum that we  do that in a way that delivers for the  British economy so people can continue  to have opportunities and job growth and  I'm confident the Prime Minister and  David Davis and the team will deliver  that and that we would do that and leave  the European Union and the customs union  as promised let's be real it's gonna be  really hard to stick to the timeframes  no civil servants are asked to go away  and come up with a plan for the customs  relationship with Europe a year ago they  came up the customs partnership that now  looks like that's for the birds we're  not gonna be ready Italian time are we  well this is supposition on where we may  end up over the conversations that going  on I've always found it best not to get  involved in hypotheticals I have great  faith in our wonderful civil service  having worked with him around things  like the piece of work we were doing to  deliver this set of status for European  citizens but they will be able to do  this work and we will be able to leave  the European Union and the customs union  as we've agreed and promised to do do  you think sometimes Teresa may just need  to ignore the people around her cabinet  table ignore the kind of cacophony on  the back benches and just make some  decisions and just get on with it - one  of the great strengths of treasom as  Prime Minister is she's promised to  going through one of the most  complicated processes this country has  seen certainly since the Second World  War in terms of leaving the European  Union and what's involved with that and  in doing that she's bringing the party  together she's bringing the country  together because obviously people in the  country of all parties voted different  ways and I think the fact that she's  working with people to do that in a  really productive way of course  delivered in December the deal that  people said couldn't be done again in  March what people said couldn't be done  that's why I'm very confident that she  will get the right deal for us as we go  forward

